## Primitive deduplication

```js
const nums   = [1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3];
const unique = [...new Set(nums)]; // [1, 2, 3]

const words   = ['apple', 'banana', 'apple', 'cherry'];
const uniqWords = [...new Set(words)]; // ['apple', 'banana', 'cherry']

// Order preserved, first occurrence wins:
const first = [...new Set([3, 1, 3, 2, 1])]; // [3, 1, 2]
```

## Why Set works

```js
const s = new Set();
s.add(1); s.add(1); s.add(2);
s.size;   // 2 — duplicates silently ignored
[...s];   // [1, 2]
```

## Object deduplication (by property)

```js
const users = [
  { id: 1, name: 'Alice' },
  { id: 2, name: 'Bob' },
  { id: 1, name: 'Alice (dup)' },
];

// Filter by first index match:
const unique = users.filter(
  (user, i, arr) => arr.findIndex(u => u.id === user.id) === i
);
// [ { id: 1, name: 'Alice' }, { id: 2, name: 'Bob' } ]

// Or Map-based (O(n) with Map lookup):
const byId = new Map(users.map(u => [u.id, u]));
const uniq = [...byId.values()];
```

